+<section aria-labelledby="exoplanets-privacy"><h2 id="exoplanets-privacy">Your exoplanet collection</h2><p>If you mark favourite systems or planets you know in Exoplanets, your selection stays in this browser until you delete it. It is not sent to Iris Green. You can save it to a file, open a saved collection or remove it using “Delete my collection” in Exoplanets. Deleting it affects only that collection.</p></section><section aria-labelledby="interests-privacy"><h2 id="interests-privacy">Your lists in Night sky, Planets and the Solar System and Eclipses</h2><p>In Night sky (“My sky”), in Planets and the Solar System and in Eclipses (“My collection”) you can mark what you have seen or want to see. That list is kept only in this browser until you delete it. It is not sent to Iris Green. You can save it to a file, open a saved file or remove it with the delete button on each page. Deleting it affects only the list on that page.</p><p>In Eclipses, the “Use my location” button asks the browser for your position only when you press it. The position is used on the page to work out the eclipse and is neither stored nor sent.</p></section></main>
